  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q71-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "71",
    "prompt": "Solve $4^x+4^{-x}-5(2^x+2^{-x})+6=0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p27-q71-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x=\\log_2(2+\\sqrt3)\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\log_2(2-\\sqrt3)",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p27-q71-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "u=2^x+2^{-x}\\ge2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " to obtain a quadratic, then solve ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "2^x+2^{-x}=4",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $u=2^x+2^{-x}$. Since $2^x>0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}u-2&=\\frac{(2^x-1)^2}{2^x}\\ge0\\\\u^2&=4^x+2+4^{-x}.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $u\\ge2$, and the equation becomes\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-2-5u+6&=0\\\\u^2-5u+4&=0\\\\(u-1)(u-4)&=0\\\\u&=1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad u=4.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $u=1$, since $u\\ge2$. Let $t=2^x>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}t+\\frac1t&=4\\\\t^2-4t+1&=0\\\\t&=\\frac{4\\pm\\sqrt{16-4}}2\\\\t&=2\\pm\\sqrt3.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are positive.\n$$\\begin{align*}2^x&=2\\pm\\sqrt3\\\\x&=\\log_2(2\\pm\\sqrt3).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
